WEBVTT

00:12.095 --> 00:16.015
‎Gyro Zeppeli finishes!

00:16.766 --> 00:20.937
‎We have our first stage champion!

00:29.028 --> 00:31.823
‎Gyro, you really took first…

00:32.699 --> 00:34.492
‎The key to his victory

00:35.493 --> 00:36.828
‎was that Spin!

00:38.121 --> 00:39.956
‎Well done, Valkyrie.

00:40.582 --> 00:43.293
‎I have to win this race, you know.

00:43.918 --> 00:46.796
‎I'll be counting on you.

00:47.922 --> 00:49.632
‎Gyro Zeppeli…

00:50.216 --> 00:53.303
‎I hear he's kept his identity
‎a complete secret.

00:53.803 --> 00:56.305
‎Authorities say

00:56.306 --> 00:59.601
‎he came to the US
‎from Genoa, Italy, this May.

01:01.019 --> 01:02.686
‎He's a foreigner?

01:02.687 --> 01:05.689
‎Yes. Apparently, he came aboard a ship

01:05.690 --> 01:07.817
‎owned by a European imperial family.

01:08.401 --> 01:09.569
‎Mr. Steel!

01:10.153 --> 01:11.863
‎A decision has been reached!

01:12.906 --> 01:14.074
‎Why?

01:14.574 --> 01:17.493
‎How could this happen?

01:17.494 --> 01:21.790
‎I'm supposed to be
‎the one-in-five-billion lucky guy!

01:22.373 --> 01:24.458
‎I'm not in first…

01:24.459 --> 01:25.876
‎Damn it.

01:25.877 --> 01:27.253
‎I, Dio…

01:29.255 --> 01:31.381
‎Would you like some food?

01:31.382 --> 01:33.134
‎It's free for all competitors.

01:34.844 --> 01:37.055
‎Looks like the guy at the start.

01:37.555 --> 01:39.140
‎But a different one?

01:40.308 --> 01:41.601
‎I'll take some.

01:45.772 --> 01:47.065
‎Just as you said.

01:47.649 --> 01:49.442
‎First off, congratulations.

01:50.860 --> 01:52.528
‎Thanks.

01:52.529 --> 01:54.947
‎But how can you be so carefree?

01:54.948 --> 01:56.616
‎You're a competitor too.

01:57.742 --> 02:00.494
‎Ladies and gentlemen,
‎thank you for waiting!

02:00.495 --> 02:03.372
‎Here are the first stage standings!

02:03.373 --> 02:06.793
‎After careful deliberation, the winner is,

02:07.585 --> 02:10.629
‎Saddlecloth number 990,

02:10.630 --> 02:11.756
‎Sand Man!

02:29.190 --> 02:31.526
‎STEEL BALL RUN
‎JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE

03:46.559 --> 03:47.893
‎#02 THE SHERIFF'S REQUEST
‎TO MOUNTAIN TIM

03:47.894 --> 03:48.977
‎The winner? Him?

03:48.978 --> 03:50.979
‎Wasn't Gyro first?

03:50.980 --> 03:52.689
‎Quiet, please!

03:52.690 --> 03:55.567
‎Our balloon observers confirmed
‎that Gyro Zeppeli

03:55.568 --> 03:58.779
‎used a weapon
‎to interfere with another competitor!

03:58.780 --> 04:02.491
‎It happened at the downhill's end,
‎just before the final turn!

04:02.492 --> 04:03.826
‎The downhill?

04:05.954 --> 04:07.247
‎That part!

04:08.790 --> 04:13.585
‎Therefore, Gyro Zeppeli
‎receives a twenty-place penalty!

04:13.586 --> 04:16.381
‎Everyone below him moves up accordingly!

04:18.132 --> 04:19.384
‎Diego's in second!

04:20.093 --> 04:21.594
‎Pocoloco's in third.

04:22.095 --> 04:25.764
‎More importantly,
‎Mountain Tim took fourth!

04:25.765 --> 04:28.559
‎He got his horse's nose across the line!

04:29.644 --> 04:31.771
‎What's wrong, Slow Dancer?

04:33.356 --> 04:34.440
‎Mountain Tim…

04:35.608 --> 04:38.611
‎A legendary cowboy
‎renowned throughout the Old West.

04:39.445 --> 04:41.239
‎I've heard the stories.

04:42.115 --> 04:45.827
‎They say every horse
‎bows its head to him out of respect.

04:55.211 --> 04:58.840
‎Mr. Steel, congratulations
‎on a successful first stage.

04:59.465 --> 05:00.716
‎Thank you.

05:00.717 --> 05:02.135
‎When's the next stage?

05:17.317 --> 05:19.944
‎Got something to say, Mr. Zeppeli?

05:20.528 --> 05:22.487
‎You should've been disqualified.

05:22.488 --> 05:24.115
‎You interfered using a weapon.

05:28.786 --> 05:30.495
‎No complaints.

05:30.496 --> 05:33.081
‎What's done is done.

05:33.082 --> 05:35.752
‎No point arguing about it now.

05:36.711 --> 05:38.545
‎I just came here

05:38.546 --> 05:41.132
‎to blow off some steam for tomorrow.

05:41.758 --> 05:44.427
‎You go celebrate with your champagne.

05:45.344 --> 05:46.554
‎Hey, wait!

05:50.641 --> 05:51.642
‎What?

05:56.898 --> 05:58.648
‎What's going on?

05:58.649 --> 06:01.402
‎I had all that champagne
‎imported from France!

06:09.911 --> 06:12.079
‎What's happening?

06:12.080 --> 06:13.289
‎Mr. Steel.

06:14.499 --> 06:16.083
‎Sheriff?

06:16.084 --> 06:18.168
‎May I have a word?

06:18.169 --> 06:19.796
‎It's a private matter.

06:20.797 --> 06:22.799
‎I'm feeling a little better now.

06:23.633 --> 06:27.470
‎So you coming along for the next stage?

06:27.970 --> 06:29.388
‎Johnny Joestar.

06:30.973 --> 06:33.935
‎Of course. I'm going to beat you.

06:36.020 --> 06:37.145
‎Very well.

06:37.146 --> 06:41.901
‎Lesson two is:
‎don't let your muscles know.

06:42.860 --> 06:44.152
‎Listen.

06:44.153 --> 06:47.240
‎The tighter you grip your arm like this,

06:47.824 --> 06:51.326
‎the more your muscles sense the force
‎and try to resist it.

06:51.327 --> 06:54.412
‎Your body instinctively
‎tries to protect itself

06:54.413 --> 06:56.623
‎because your muscles detect it.

06:56.624 --> 06:58.501
‎That's how every living body works.

06:59.293 --> 07:01.628
‎The Spin never lets the muscles know.

07:01.629 --> 07:02.964
‎Control the skin.

07:03.464 --> 07:07.300
‎As long as it's only skin-deep,
‎the muscles won't know.

07:07.301 --> 07:09.928
‎Control the skin? What do you--

07:09.929 --> 07:12.264
‎Want to try? If you're game.

07:12.265 --> 07:16.269
‎The champagne cork in your hand
‎is already spinning.

07:31.659 --> 07:33.535
‎That's how you get off a horse.

07:33.536 --> 07:35.913
‎The horse's muscles never knew.

07:36.497 --> 07:40.459
‎That movement
‎used the opposite spin from when I got on.

07:40.460 --> 07:42.127
‎Don't let the muscles know.

07:42.128 --> 07:45.840
‎The weapon isn't the Steel Ball itself.
‎It's the power of the Spin.

07:46.549 --> 07:50.051
‎Johnny Joestar, we'll cross
‎the desert in the second stage.

07:50.052 --> 07:51.971
‎It's over 700 miles.

07:52.472 --> 07:53.848
‎It's going to be tough.

07:54.348 --> 07:56.725
‎Let's form an alliance.

07:56.726 --> 07:59.479
‎We'll finish one-two!

08:02.064 --> 08:04.400
‎I'll be the one, though.

08:08.321 --> 08:11.615
‎What is this?

08:11.616 --> 08:16.244
‎As you can see,
‎there's been a murder, Mr. Steel.

08:16.245 --> 08:19.456
‎Someone murdered them during the race.

08:19.457 --> 08:23.043
‎Over 3,000 competitors
‎were riding alongside them,

08:23.044 --> 08:25.170
‎yet no one saw a thing.

08:25.171 --> 08:28.632
‎Don't be ridiculous!
‎What possible motive--

08:28.633 --> 08:31.134
‎The motive? 50 million dollars.

08:31.135 --> 08:33.054
‎To move up in the standings.

08:34.138 --> 08:37.224
‎Every competitor is a suspect.

08:37.225 --> 08:39.601
‎At this rate, there'll be more victims.

08:39.602 --> 08:43.231
‎Will you suspend the race
‎while we investigate?

08:44.690 --> 08:45.774
‎No!

08:45.775 --> 08:50.279
‎This race has grown beyond my own will.

08:50.863 --> 08:52.447
‎I thought as much.

08:52.448 --> 08:54.909
‎Steven. You're…

08:59.664 --> 09:02.416
‎Their scent has a calming effect.

09:03.626 --> 09:06.754
‎Please accept them, Mrs. Steel.

09:12.301 --> 09:17.181
‎I understand how concerned you are
‎for your beloved husband.

09:17.765 --> 09:19.767
‎Rest assured. Leave it to me.

09:22.979 --> 09:25.855
‎Is he Mountain Tim?

09:25.856 --> 09:27.232
‎What's he doing here?

09:27.233 --> 09:29.859
‎I sent for him

09:29.860 --> 09:32.362
‎to track down the killer.

09:32.363 --> 09:33.446
‎Track the killer?

09:33.447 --> 09:35.740
‎But he's a competitor!

09:35.741 --> 09:37.326
‎That is why.

09:37.827 --> 09:40.954
‎He could be the killer's next target.

09:40.955 --> 09:43.582
‎In that case, let him track the killer.

09:43.583 --> 09:45.417
‎You sure ask a lot of a man.

09:45.418 --> 09:50.338
‎Mr. Steel, I'd like to appoint him
‎as my deputy.

09:50.339 --> 09:52.758
‎Only if that's acceptable to you.

09:56.012 --> 09:57.471
‎This is terrible.

09:58.139 --> 10:02.226
‎I can't even think about winning
‎with someone like this around.

10:03.060 --> 10:06.731
‎A lot of my friends
‎are racing in this too.

10:11.193 --> 10:14.822
‎If I'm tracking footprints,
‎this is the one.

10:15.948 --> 10:18.951
‎This one must be the most aggressive.

10:19.535 --> 10:22.537
‎The horseshoe has a V-shaped chip
‎in the center.

10:22.538 --> 10:23.831
‎What?

10:24.332 --> 10:26.166
‎The horse was agitated.

10:26.167 --> 10:28.294
‎Because it saw human blood.

10:28.794 --> 10:32.423
‎The rider's methodical.
‎Must've been raised in the desert.

10:33.424 --> 10:35.176
‎A bottle beside the victim?

10:36.510 --> 10:38.429
‎There's something inside.

10:39.805 --> 10:41.599
‎Is that a button?

10:49.565 --> 10:52.651
‎Does it have something to do
‎with the murder?

10:52.652 --> 10:54.528
‎It's from the victim's jeans.

10:55.738 --> 10:57.781
‎Why did the button come off

10:57.782 --> 11:00.034
‎and end up inside the bottle?

11:00.826 --> 11:02.077
‎One thing's certain.

11:02.078 --> 11:07.583
‎It's dangerous to let anyone get close
‎without knowing who they are.

11:14.590 --> 11:16.967
‎SEPTEMBER 26, 1890
‎SANTA MARIA NOVELLA CHURCH

11:18.469 --> 11:20.637
‎Five minutes to the start!

11:20.638 --> 11:25.351
‎The second stage is
‎a long-distance race of roughly 750 miles.

11:25.935 --> 11:28.728
‎It should take about two weeks.

11:28.729 --> 11:31.856
‎From here, they'll cross
‎the Arizona desert

11:31.857 --> 11:33.776
‎and finish at Monument Valley.

11:34.276 --> 11:36.820
‎As long as they pass the checkpoints,

11:36.821 --> 11:39.240
‎their routes are entirely up to them!

11:40.199 --> 11:43.828
‎Gyro, Sand Man's the favorite
‎to win this stage.

11:44.412 --> 11:46.746
‎The betting's on. He's the favorite.

11:46.747 --> 11:47.998
‎What do you think?

11:48.916 --> 11:50.708
‎Not me?

11:50.709 --> 11:52.043
‎Afraid not.

11:52.044 --> 11:54.504
‎For the record, I'm sixth.

11:54.505 --> 11:56.256
‎And you're ninth.

11:56.257 --> 11:58.258
‎What do they know?

11:58.259 --> 12:00.677
‎The general public.

12:00.678 --> 12:03.138
‎Not that I care.

12:03.139 --> 12:05.557
‎Mountain Tim, over there…

12:05.558 --> 12:08.852
‎He's a favorite to win too.

12:08.853 --> 12:10.311
‎There you go.

12:10.312 --> 12:13.022
‎He's got a funny hat.

12:13.023 --> 12:14.899
‎Makes me want to stomp on it.

12:14.900 --> 12:18.945
‎Before it's even off his head.

12:18.946 --> 12:23.033
‎They say Mountain Tim isn't cut out
‎for short races because he's a cowboy.

12:23.617 --> 12:26.327
‎But yesterday, he caught me by surprise.

12:26.328 --> 12:28.079
‎Then passed me before the finish.

12:28.080 --> 12:30.498
‎With a hat like that?

12:30.499 --> 12:33.793
‎And you didn't notice him? Ha, ha! Nyo-ho!

12:33.794 --> 12:35.921
‎Gyro, I think this stage

12:36.422 --> 12:38.757
‎will be a battle to find water.

12:39.550 --> 12:44.180
‎In 1875, a cavalry unit of 26 men
‎was wiped out.

12:45.097 --> 12:47.850
‎Not in battle, and not by accident.

12:48.434 --> 12:51.979
‎The usual watering hole
‎dried up that year.

12:52.480 --> 12:56.357
‎They wandered the endless desert
‎in search of water.

12:56.358 --> 12:58.277
‎They slowly baked to death

12:58.861 --> 13:01.280
‎in the scorching heat.

13:03.824 --> 13:05.242
‎This marks a watering hole.

13:05.826 --> 13:09.370
‎Day one, the first watering hole
‎isn't until mile 30.

13:09.371 --> 13:11.372
‎If we can't find it,

13:11.373 --> 13:13.459
‎we won't just retire. We'll die.

13:14.126 --> 13:17.295
‎And this cork…

13:17.296 --> 13:19.632
‎How can I make it spin?

13:22.510 --> 13:27.223
‎It's time for the second stage to begin!

13:29.016 --> 13:30.517
‎They're off!

13:30.518 --> 13:33.312
‎The Steel Ball Run's second stage
‎is under way!

13:34.855 --> 13:36.814
‎-What?
‎-He's pulling away!

13:36.815 --> 13:40.194
‎That's Gyro! Gyro Zeppeli!

13:41.403 --> 13:43.738
‎What's his problem?

13:43.739 --> 13:46.617
‎Didn't he hear what I just said?

13:48.410 --> 13:51.622
‎I'm coming! I'm right behind you!

13:55.209 --> 13:56.334
‎No way…

13:56.335 --> 13:58.503
‎What's Gyro Zeppeli doing?

13:58.504 --> 14:01.297
‎He's not just taken off.
‎He's changed his route!

14:01.298 --> 14:02.632
‎The desert?

14:02.633 --> 14:06.679
‎Is he cutting straight across
‎and ignoring the watering hole?

14:07.721 --> 14:09.138
‎Are you crazy, Gyro?

14:09.139 --> 14:11.432
‎We've got another 750 miles ahead of us!

14:11.433 --> 14:12.893
‎What are you thinking?

14:13.561 --> 14:17.063
‎We're rivals, remember?

14:17.064 --> 14:19.942
‎Wanna come? I'm taking the shortest route.

14:20.526 --> 14:22.151
‎Why wouldn't I?

14:22.152 --> 14:23.903
‎Otherwise, Sand Man

14:23.904 --> 14:25.990
‎or someone else will beat us.

14:26.657 --> 14:28.032
‎Damn it!

14:28.033 --> 14:29.492
‎Wow!

14:29.493 --> 14:32.537
‎Gyro's not alone!
‎Other competitors are following him

14:32.538 --> 14:33.955
‎into the desert!

14:33.956 --> 14:37.208
‎No sane competitor
‎would choose that route!

14:37.209 --> 14:39.795
‎Do they have a death wish?

14:56.020 --> 14:59.315
‎There are no railroad tracks
‎beyond this point.

14:59.899 --> 15:01.983
‎The train will go on ahead

15:01.984 --> 15:04.236
‎and wait at the checkpoints.

15:05.237 --> 15:08.115
‎6 HOURS LATER

15:08.866 --> 15:10.159
‎Who's that?

15:10.743 --> 15:12.911
‎What's hanging from his ear?

15:12.912 --> 15:14.830
‎I can't tell through the dust.

15:15.664 --> 15:19.335
‎According to his saddlecloth number,
‎his name's Robinson.

15:19.919 --> 15:22.129
‎He's about 150 lengths behind us.

15:23.213 --> 15:24.505
‎Hey, Gyro.

15:24.506 --> 15:26.382
‎We've been riding for six hours.

15:26.383 --> 15:28.718
‎We're still headed the right way, right?

15:28.719 --> 15:31.220
‎50 miles to the watering hole.

15:31.221 --> 15:33.599
‎Sorry to keep asking,
‎but are we still right?

15:34.350 --> 15:39.980
‎There isn't any mountain like that
‎on this map.

15:45.486 --> 15:48.864
‎Yep! We're right on course.
‎Everything's perfect!

15:49.365 --> 15:50.866
‎-Probably.
‎-What?

15:51.659 --> 15:54.202
‎Did you just say "probably"?

15:54.203 --> 15:56.371
‎Don't worry.

15:56.372 --> 15:59.457
‎Other competitors are following us.
‎We're right!

15:59.458 --> 16:01.751
‎-I think.
‎-"I think"?

16:01.752 --> 16:04.045
‎We'll die if we miss that watering hole!

16:04.046 --> 16:08.633
‎I'm asking if you know anything
‎about the desert!

16:08.634 --> 16:10.927
‎I'm telling you, we're fine.

16:10.928 --> 16:13.013
‎Out here, close enough is good enough.

16:13.514 --> 16:17.100
‎More importantly,
‎have you mastered the Spin?

16:17.101 --> 16:19.561
‎The cork spin I taught you!

16:37.913 --> 16:39.455
‎What's wrong?

16:39.456 --> 16:41.542
‎Something just flew by.

16:44.211 --> 16:46.212
‎Gyro…

16:46.213 --> 16:48.465
‎Your ear…

16:57.558 --> 16:59.351
‎This is…

16:59.935 --> 17:02.270
‎Shit! My arms got cut!

17:02.271 --> 17:05.190
‎It's ahead!
‎Something's coming from up ahead!

17:08.777 --> 17:12.697
‎He's on the move.
‎He's trying to catch up to us!

17:12.698 --> 17:15.408
‎Was it him? Did he do this?

17:15.409 --> 17:16.743
‎Calm down, Gyro.

17:16.744 --> 17:18.494
‎Something's wrong.

17:18.495 --> 17:20.413
‎The attack came from ahead.

17:20.414 --> 17:22.206
‎Get behind those rocks.

17:22.207 --> 17:24.250
‎Don't move the horses too much.

17:24.251 --> 17:27.253
‎Gyro, these are cactus spines.

17:27.254 --> 17:29.464
‎You know a lot about the desert?

17:29.465 --> 17:30.965
‎A little.

17:30.966 --> 17:34.135
‎Some desert cactuses shoot their spines.

17:34.136 --> 17:35.637
‎They're called chollas.

17:36.221 --> 17:37.930
‎When an animal gets close,

17:37.931 --> 17:40.934
‎they sense vibrations
‎and fire their spines.

17:43.729 --> 17:45.981
‎Damn. Those must be chollas.

17:46.482 --> 17:48.983
‎They're growing all over the place.

17:48.984 --> 17:51.778
‎So which is it?

17:51.779 --> 17:55.199
‎Are we the ones at fault
‎for riding into this cactus patch?

17:55.699 --> 17:58.910
‎Or is he the bad guy,

17:58.911 --> 18:01.162
‎using the cactuses against us?

18:01.163 --> 18:02.455
‎I don't know.

18:02.456 --> 18:06.293
‎You'd have to get pretty close
‎to make a cholla fire its spines.

18:06.877 --> 18:08.503
‎He's much too far away.

18:08.504 --> 18:11.757
‎But he's definitely got a motive.

18:12.341 --> 18:17.221
‎He can use the cactuses to take us out
‎without penalty.

18:18.472 --> 18:19.722
‎He's coming around!

18:19.723 --> 18:21.933
‎But we don't know if he did it.

18:21.934 --> 18:24.685
‎Damn it!
‎We've got to get out of this area.

18:24.686 --> 18:26.187
‎Let's ride, Johnny!

18:26.188 --> 18:27.606
‎Right! Gyro!

18:32.069 --> 18:33.402
‎The reins were cut!

18:33.403 --> 18:35.989
‎No way! They cut the reins!

18:37.866 --> 18:39.243
‎It's impossibly accurate!

18:49.211 --> 18:50.545
‎Get on your horse!

18:50.546 --> 18:52.548
‎This is definitely his doing!

18:58.470 --> 19:00.138
‎Go on ahead!

19:00.139 --> 19:02.891
‎Blood got in my eyes,
‎but my eyes are fine!

19:03.600 --> 19:04.934
‎Go!

19:04.935 --> 19:07.645
‎We promised
‎we'd make it to the finish together,

19:07.646 --> 19:09.188
‎but a race is a race.

19:09.189 --> 19:10.898
‎Don't wait for me.

19:10.899 --> 19:13.277
‎I'll catch up once I wipe the blood off!

19:16.947 --> 19:19.073
‎All right. I'll go on ahead.

19:19.074 --> 19:20.242
‎Yeah! Go!

19:20.826 --> 19:21.827
‎But…

19:22.619 --> 19:25.747
‎I'm heading toward that bastard!

19:32.087 --> 19:35.923
‎Gyro! Your Steel Ball
‎is considered a weapon!

19:35.924 --> 19:38.593
‎And there's no proof he's behind this.

19:38.594 --> 19:42.555
‎If you attack him now,
‎you'll be disqualified!

19:42.556 --> 19:45.766
‎You should just get out of this area!

19:45.767 --> 19:48.645
‎You should just stay in the race!

19:55.736 --> 20:00.239
‎In one desert village, whenever a dispute
‎turned into a fight to the death,

20:00.240 --> 20:04.369
‎the loser would be chained to a cactus
‎and left there to die.

20:04.953 --> 20:07.038
‎I grew up in a village like that.

20:07.039 --> 20:10.083
‎I mastered a skill
‎so no one could ever control me.

20:10.667 --> 20:14.379
‎To make sure I never lose,
‎I keep insects inside my body.

20:15.339 --> 20:17.924
‎Using the airflow
‎from their high-speed flight,

20:17.925 --> 20:21.887
‎I can shoot cholla spines
‎exactly where I want!

20:25.599 --> 20:28.851
‎Now that you know my secret,

20:28.852 --> 20:30.144
‎take this.

20:30.145 --> 20:33.522
‎No one is getting ahead of me
‎in this race!

20:33.523 --> 20:34.399
‎Nyo-ho!

20:35.025 --> 20:38.277
‎Then we're thinking along the same lines.

20:38.278 --> 20:41.322
‎You thought I just dropped my Steel Balls?

20:41.323 --> 20:44.785
‎My precious Steel Balls on the ground?

20:46.620 --> 20:50.122
‎What's that buzzing?

20:50.123 --> 20:53.877
‎It's not my insects, is it?

20:54.461 --> 20:57.505
‎I'm not that accurate.

20:57.506 --> 21:00.216
‎But the Spin's vibrations reached you.

21:00.217 --> 21:02.636
‎They spread through the ground around you.

21:03.595 --> 21:06.723
‎I'll keep my distance.
‎Don't wanna get caught in that.

21:16.942 --> 21:18.860
‎It wasn't me.

21:22.656 --> 21:23.949
‎The cactus did it.

21:25.617 --> 21:27.869
‎That cost us more time than I expected.

21:28.453 --> 21:31.373
‎Come on, Johnny. Let's get moving.

21:32.541 --> 21:34.543
‎Right. Gyro.

23:11.306 --> 23:12.390
‎That's…

23:13.308 --> 23:14.893
‎Robinson.

23:17.729 --> 23:19.605
‎It's not him.

23:19.606 --> 23:22.024
‎The killer I'm after

23:22.025 --> 23:23.652
‎has a different horseshoe.

23:24.277 --> 23:26.404
‎But I'm still on the right trail.

23:27.072 --> 23:30.408
‎The chipped horseshoe
‎came through here already.

23:31.409 --> 23:33.328
‎About 30 minutes ago, I'd say.

23:33.912 --> 23:35.914
‎Subtitle translation by: Ryoko Quirke
